cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Brain Typing: Converting Your Thoughts to Texts via Deep Feature Learning of EEG Signals"
abstract: >
  A unified deep learning framework that leverages a joint convolutional recurrent neural
  network to classify motor imagery EEG signals for brain-computer interface typing. The
  model fuses CNN-extracted spatial features, RNN-captured temporal dependencies, and an
  autoencoder layer for robustness to incomplete or corrupted signals. An XGBoost classifier
  operates on the fused representations. The system achieves 95.53% classification accuracy
  on a large-scale public EEG dataset and a lab-collected Emotiv dataset.
